08","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111815#issuecomment-3491180508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111815","id":3491180508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QFy_c","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T13:19:51Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05T13:24:27Z","body":"Since the performance loss was less than expected, I set the default for `mutable_bone_axes` to true as it resolves the Gizmo issue with the root bone mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110120 's description.\r\n\r\n> Known issue\r\nMoving the position breaks the rendering of the Limitation gizmo because binding to position alone is impossible. To fix it, an approach such as canceling rotation within the shader like https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9735 is required. Currently, it is drawn by a hack to bind the limitation to the parent joint. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111815.\r\n\r\nAlthough it could potentially be non-optional (debatable).\r\n\r\nInstead, 